  type: project\n  originSessionId: cef69ec2-8b5a-4e91-8078-ac955e039295\n  modified: 2026-07-27T07:05:06.329Z\n---\n\nPer-turn agent provenance shipped in cledger 0.12.0 (PR #1, branch\n`worktree-producer-metadata`, draft as of 2026-07-27). Closes the `Producer`\ngap the 0.10.0 reasoning entry flagged as out of scope.\n\n**Shape:** three optional fields — `producer.model`, `producer.provider`,\n`producer.source_version` (the coding CLI's own version; `producer.version`\nremains cledger's). Plus `cledger log --model M` and a model column in\n`cledger conversations`.\n\n**Decisions (so they don't get re-litigated):**\n- *Only what the source states.* `provider` stays unset for claude-code (never\n  named in the transcript; the CLI can point at Bedrock/Vertex). A model is\n  never carried onto a turn the source didn't label, so claude-code user turns\n  have no model. `\"<synthetic>\"` passes through verbatim.\n- *Excluded from event identity.* Added after events existed without them, so\n  including them would make a rescan duplicate every pre-upgrade turn instead\n  of deduping.\n- *Forward-only, no backfill command.* Rewriting `producer` keeps ids but\n  changes note lines; under `cat_sort_uniq` the rewritten and original both\n  survive a merge with a peer holding the old one. Old claude-code events keep\n  the data in `raw.data`; old codex events lost it for good.\n- *Out of scope:* the rest of codex's `session_meta`/`turn_context` payload —\n  `base_instructions` (full system prompt), sandbox/approval policy, reasoning\n  effort. Whole-session configuration is a separate question with its own size\n  and redaction implications.\n\n**Codex-specific gotcha worth remembering:** `turn_context` is written *after*\nthe turn's opening messages in real rollouts (verified on a live file — line\norder was session_meta, response_items, then turn_context). A strictly-forward\nrule leaves the first user message of every session unlabelled, so unset fields\nare seeded from the earliest line stating them ahead. Synthetic fixtures passed\nbefore this was caught against real data.\n\nSee [[project-cledger-reasoning-preservation]] — this gap mattered most there,\nsince an encrypted blob is only replayable against the model that produced it.\n","filePath":"/Users/evintunador/.claude/projects/-Users-evintunador-repos-evintunador-conversation-ledger/memory/project-cledger-agent-provenance.md","memdirStamped":true,"originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[],"type":"create","userModified":false},"type":"user","userType":"external","uuid":"51a9abc8-1f00-416d-ba32-f93985e72666","version":"2.1.220"},"format":"claude-code-jsonl/1"},"recorded_at":"2026-07-27T07:19:34.708Z","schema":"conversation-ledger/v1"}
