ssage of every session unlabelled. Still-unset fields are now seeded from the earliest line stating them ahead — not a guess, since the first stated context is by construction the first turn's, and the only items preceding it belong to that same turn. Seeding fills gaps only, so a genuine mid-session model switch still applies forward and never retroactively.\n\n## Identity and backfill\n\nThe fields are **excluded from the event identity subset**. They're source-determined and stable, but they were added after events existed without them — folding them into the id would give the same transcript line a different id before and after the upgrade, so a rescan would duplicate every pre-upgrade turn instead of deduping it.\n\n**Forward-only, deliberately no backfill.** Rewriting `producer` on stored events would keep their ids (it's outside the identity subset) but change their serialized note lines, and under `cat_sort_uniq` the rewritten and original lines would both survive a merge with any peer still holding the old one — two copies of one event. Old claude-code events lose nothing permanent (their whole source line is in `raw.data`); old codex events do, and re-capturing doesn't help since they dedup by id.\n\nScanning is unaffected: `cledger scan` and capture-tier redaction walk only `content` and `raw.data`, so model ids and version strings aren't pattern-matched.\n\n## Verification\n\n- 144 tests, 143 pass, 1 pre-existing skip. Six new tests cover both adapter shapes, the cursor-resume path, the trailing-`turn_context` case, identity stability, and the `--model` filter.\n- Verified end to end against a **real** codex rollout and a real claude-code transcript, not just fixtures — the trailing-`turn_context` gap was found that way, after synthetic fixtures passed.\n- `cledger scan` clean; `tsc --noEmit` clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01ALwbJRNasvVmw2jBkdkgkt\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -3","descr