{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"Done. Sanity checks: `tsc --noEmit` clean, 144 tests (143 pass, 1 pre-existing skip, 6 new), build clean, `cledger scan` clean, and I re-captured a real codex rollout and a real claude-code transcript to confirm the fields populate on live data rather than only fixtures.\n\n## What shipped (0.12.0, PR #1, draft)\n\nThree optional `producer` fields — `model`, `provider`, `source_version` (the coding CLI's own version; `producer.version` stays cledger's) — plus `cledger log --model M` and a model column in `cledger conversations`.\n\n**Only what the source states.** `provider` stays unset for claude-code, since the transcript never names one and the same CLI can point at Bedrock or Vertex. A model is never carried onto a turn the source didn't label, so claude-code user turns have none. `\"<synthetic>\"` passes through verbatim.\n\n**Codex was where the actual work was.** Its facts live on out-of-band `session_meta`/`turn_context` lines, which forced two fixes. A cursor-resumed capture never re-reads those lines, so the adapter now re-scans the file prefix to rebuild the context in force. And — this one only showed up against real data — codex writes `turn_context` *after* the turn's opening messages, so my first implementation left the first user message of every session unlabelled even though synthetic fixtures passed. Still-unset fields are now seeded from the earliest line stating them ahead; seeding fills gaps only, so a genuine mid-session model switch still applies forward and never retroactively.\n\n**Identity and backfill.** The fields are excluded from the event identity subset — folding them in would make a rescan duplicate every pre-upgrade turn instead of deduping it. Forward-only with no backfill command, deliberately: rewriting `producer` on stored events keeps their ids but changes their note lines, and under `cat_sort_uniq` the rewritten and original would both survive a merge with a peer holding the old one. Old claude-code events lose nothing permanent (their whole line is in `raw.data`); old codex events do.\n\nI left codex's `base_instructions`, sandbox policy, and reasoning effort uncaptured — that's whole-session configuration with its own size and redaction implications, noted in the roadmap as separate rather than quietly folded in.\n\n## One thing you should know about, unrelated to this change\n\n`cledger scan` reported 213 findings from the worktree but 0 from your main checkout. Cause: `findRepo` derives `gitDir` from `git rev-parse --absolute-git-dir`, which in a worktree returns `.git/worktrees/<name>/`. All per-repo local state hangs off that path — allowlist, known-secrets, cursors, pending queue — so none of it is visible from a worktree, and every already-allowlisted finding reappears. Cursors reset too, so a capture from a worktree can re-scan transcripts from the top. Pre-existing and unrelated to this work, so I didn't fix it; the likely fix is `--git-common-dir`, but that needs a decision about which state is genuinely shared vs. per-worktree rather than a blind swap. Saved to memory.\n\nresult: cledger 0.12.0 records per-turn model/provider/CLI-version in `producer` — draft PR #1 open at https://github.com/evintunador/conversation-ledger/pull/1, 143 tests passing, verified against real codex and claude-code transcripts; separately flagged a pre-existing bug where cledger's allowlist and cursors are invisible from a git worktree.","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"8edda189e36c819dec24702a4720f65a3a54c6fb","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:cef69ec2-8b5a-4e91-8078-ac955e039295","seq":485},"id":"ev1-cbbf3b817a3f56910d380aa72faa3e6f457050a1b7c823ce0b952209340bc2cc","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-27T07:05:40.076Z","producer":{"model":"claude